  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ES-C13-plurales-cambio",
      "sequence": 1186,
      "title": "queremos, quieren — work them out first",
      "headword": "queremos · quieren",
      "romanization": "queremos · quieren",
      "gloss": "the stem-changers in the plural — and you can work them out before you are told",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:d799c51a996f6bd7",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before you read on: you have the singular of querer, and you have the stem-change rule. What is \"we want\"? Say your answer out loud, then continue."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: you were right",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "queremos — we want., quieren — they want. podemos — we can., pueden — they can."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "If you said queremos rather than quieremos, you did not remember it. You derived it, from a rule you were given one chapter ago: the stem breaks exactly where it is stressed, so nosotros never breaks."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And quieren breaks, because there the stress is back on the stem."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is the difference between a course that hands you tables and one that hands you rules. Four forms you had never seen, and none of them needed teaching."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A test you can run yourself. You have puedo and puedes. Without being told, what are we can and they can?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the yo, nosotros and ellos forms of querer — break, no break, break",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the *yo*, *nosotros* and *ellos* forms of *querer* — break, no break, break]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the same three for poder",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the same three for *poder*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C13-plurales-cambio-want",
              "prompt": "We want.",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-QUERER-PRESENT-PLURAL"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "queremos",
                "nosotros queremos"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Yes — no break, because the stress moved.",
                "incorrect": "queremos. The stem only breaks under stress."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C13-plurales-cambio-can",
              "prompt": "They can.",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-PODER-PRESENT-PLURAL"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "pueden",
                "ellos pueden",
                "ustedes pueden"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Yes — the break is back, because the stress is.",
                "incorrect": "pueden."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C13-plurales-cambio-derive",
              "prompt": "Poder changes o to ue. What is we can?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-STEM-CHANGE-STRESS-RULE"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 10,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "podemos",
                "nosotros podemos"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Right — and you derived it rather than recalled it.",
                "incorrect": "podemos. Nosotros never breaks."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is \"we want\"? (Queremos.) Why no break? (The stress is on the ending.) And could you have produced these without this lesson? (Yes — which is the point of it.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-C13-plurales-yo-go",
      "sequence": 1187,
      "title": "hacemos, hacen — and the club has no plural at all",
      "headword": "hacemos · hacen",
      "romanization": "hacemos · hacen",
      "gloss": "the -go verbs in the plural — where the oddity simply is not",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:889b5b78e3a53f91",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Name the six -go verbs. And say where in each one the -go appears."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: an oddity that was only ever in one slot",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You were told, when the club closed, that the -go lives in the yo form and nowhere else. Here is what that is worth:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hacemos, hacéis, hacen — plain -er endings. ponemos, ponéis, ponen — plain -er endings. salimos, salís, salen — plain -ir endings."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nothing to learn. The -go club has no plural forms of its own, because the thing that made it a club was never in the plural to begin with."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two of the six do something in the plural, and it is not the -go:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "decimos but dicen, venimos but vienen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Those are stem changes, and they follow the rule you already have — the stem breaks where it is stressed, and nosotros is never stressed on the stem. So even the exceptions are not exceptions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two rules — the -go is yo-only, and stems break under stress — now generate the entire present tense of every irregular verb in this book, in every person."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is what a rule buys that a table does not: the table stops at the forms printed on it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "all six -go verbs in the we form — and hear that none is odd",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: all six *-go* verbs in the *we* form — and hear that none is odd]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "\"decimos, dicen\" and \"venimos, vienen\" — the two that break, and why",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"decimos, dicen\" and \"venimos, vienen\" — the two that break, and why]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C13-plurales-yo-go-we",
              "prompt": "We do or make.",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-YO-GO-PLURAL-REGULAR"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "hacemos",
                "nosotros hacemos"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Yes — a plain -er ending.",
                "incorrect": "hacemos."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C13-plurales-yo-go-out",
              "prompt": "They leave.",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-SALIR-PRESENT-SINGULAR",
                "ES-GRAMMAR-YO-GO-PLURAL-REGULAR"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "salen",
                "ellos salen",
                "ustedes salen"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Yes — no -go anywhere in the plural.",
                "incorrect": "salen."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C13-plurales-yo-go-say",
              "prompt": "Decir stem-changes. What are we say and they say?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-STEM-CHANGE-STRESS-RULE"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 10,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "decimos and dicen",
                "decimos, dicen"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Right — nosotros never breaks, they does.",
                "incorrect": "decimos and dicen."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "How many special plural forms does the -go club have? (None — the -go was only ever in yo.) Which two do something in the plural, and what? (Decir and venir — a stem change, following the stress.) How many rules now generate every irregular present in this book? (Two.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-C13-sintesis-derivar",
      "sequence": 1188,
      "title": "Synthesis — a verb you have never met",
      "headword": "(synthesis)",
      "romanization": "(synthesis)",
      "gloss": "synthesis — conjugate a verb this book has never shown you",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:539a347dc080e30d",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nothing new in this chapter, and nothing to memorise. Say the six endings of a regular -er verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Everything you hold about the present tense now fits in three lines:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three families, six endings each; -er and -ir differ only in nosotros and vosotros."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A stem breaks exactly where it is stressed — so nosotros and vosotros never break."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A -go sits in the yo form and nowhere else."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is the whole system. Not a summary of it — the system."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And a system, unlike a table, works on words it has never seen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "The exchange",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here is a verb this book has not taught you: beber, \"to drink\" — you have met the word, but never its full set."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Do not look anything up. It is a regular -er verb, so:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "bebo, bebes, bebe, bebemos, bebéis, beben."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Six forms, and the only thing you needed was rule 1."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now one that uses all three rules. Salir is an -ir verb, and it is in the -go club. Rules 1 and 3 give you every form, and you can produce them before reading on:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "salgo, sales, sale, salimos, salís, salen."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One odd form, in the one slot rule 3 names. The other five are plain -ir."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four broken, two whole, and the two whole ones are the two the stress leaves alone. Every time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "all six of beber, without looking",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: all six of *beber*, without looking]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "all six of salir, and name the only odd one",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: all six of *salir*, and name the only odd one]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Until deriving is faster than remembering."
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C13-sintesis-derivar-count",
              "prompt": "Salir is a -go verb. What is we leave?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-STEM-CHANGE-STRESS-RULE"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 10,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "salimos",
                "nosotros salimos"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Right — the -go never leaves the yo slot.",
                "incorrect": "salimos, perfectly plain."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C13-sintesis-derivar-they",
              "prompt": "And they leave?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-STEM-CHANGE-STRESS-RULE"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "salen",
                "ellos salen"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Yes — nothing odd outside yo.",
                "incorrect": "salen."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C13-sintesis-derivar-rules",
              "prompt": "How many rules generate the whole present tense?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-PRESENT-INDICATIVE-COMPLETE",
                "ES-GRAMMAR-YO-GO-PLURAL-REGULAR"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "three",
                "3",
                "tres"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Three — families, stress, and the yo-only -go.",
                "incorrect": "Three."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "State the three rules. (Three families, stems break under stress, the -go is yo-only.) Which two forms never break? (Nosotros, vosotros.) And what can you do now that a table could not give you? (Conjugate a verb nobody taught me.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": []
}
